.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt PLEDGE 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm pledge
.Nm unveil
.Nd restrict process capabilities and paths
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In unistd.h
.Ft int
.Fn pledge "const char *promises" "const char *execpromises"
.Ft int
.Fn unveil "const char *path" "const char *permissions"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn pledge limits the system calls a process may use. .Fn unveil limits the paths the process
may access. Both are RavenBSD compatibility interfaces.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Both functions return 0 on success and -1 on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Er EINVAL is returned for an unknown promise or permission. .Er EPERM is returned when the
process cannot tighten its own policy.
.Sh STANDARDS
OpenBSD compatibility; ring 2.
.Sh CAVEATS
The enforcement model and its current coverage are documented in C53; unsupported promises
do not silently grant access.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pledge 2
.Xr libc 7
